; Transparent canvas — port of the webgpu-samples `transparentCanvas` sample.
; The rotating cube from rotating_cube.sjon over an alpha-0 clear with the
; canvas configured premultiplied: everywhere the cube does not cover, the
; host page shows through the canvas. Upstream demonstrates this with HTML
; text behind an absolutely-positioned canvas; a PNGB payload is the canvas
; content only, so observe the effect over a non-black page (the playground
; loader page works, as does any `--html` codegen page with a styled body).
;
; This file used to say all of that by copying rotating_cube.sjon and changing
; one clear value. It says it by importing instead, which is the same claim
; written once: the cube, cleared to nothing, on a premultiplied canvas.
;
; The fragment output must be premultiplied alpha; the cube is fully opaque
; (alpha 1) so that holds trivially — the transparency is all in the clear.
; (canvas :alpha-mode premultiplied) is NOT the default — the schema follows
; GPUCanvasConfiguration.alphaMode and defaults to opaque —
; so the file that depends on it states it. Deleting the line flips the
; header's flags byte (0x08 → 0x00) and the page stops showing through. The
; alpha mode is consumed by the JS runtime at context.configure(), before the
; first opcode runs. It is declared HERE rather than rebound, because the
; imported document does not declare one at all: an import adds this
; document's own forms to the imported ones, and only `(define …)` replaces.

(import :file "./rotating_cube.sjon"
  (define :name CLEAR_LEVEL :value 0)
  (define :name CLEAR_ALPHA :value 0))

(canvas :alpha-mode premultiplied)
